  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "$S=\\{A,B,C,D,E\\}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "List all the subsets of $\\{A,B,C,D,E\\}$ containing 2 letters.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\{A,B\\},\\ \\{A,C\\},\\ \\{A,D\\},\\ \\{A,E\\},\\ \\{B,C\\},\\ \\{B,D\\},\\ \\{B,E\\},\\ \\{C,D\\},\\ \\{C,E\\},\\ \\{D,E\\}$. 10 subsets in total.",
          "worked": "List pairs systematically by their first letter, without repeating a pair:\n$$\\begin{aligned}&\\{A,B\\},\\ \\{A,C\\},\\ \\{A,D\\},\\ \\{A,E\\},\\\\&\\{B,C\\},\\ \\{B,D\\},\\ \\{B,E\\},\\\\&\\{C,D\\},\\ \\{C,E\\},\\ \\{D,E\\}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThere are $4+3+2+1=10$ subsets.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "List all the subsets of $\\{A,B,C,D,E\\}$ containing 3 letters.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\{A,B,C\\},\\ \\{A,B,D\\},\\ \\{A,B,E\\},\\ \\{A,C,D\\},\\ \\{A,C,E\\},\\ \\{A,D,E\\},\\ \\{B,C,D\\},\\ \\{B,C,E\\},\\ \\{B,D,E\\},\\ \\{C,D,E\\}$. 10 subsets in total.",
          "worked": "List triples systematically, without repeating a subset:\n$$\\begin{aligned}&\\{A,B,C\\},\\ \\{A,B,D\\},\\ \\{A,B,E\\},\\\\&\\{A,C,D\\},\\ \\{A,C,E\\},\\ \\{A,D,E\\},\\\\&\\{B,C,D\\},\\ \\{B,C,E\\},\\ \\{B,D,E\\},\\\\&\\{C,D,E\\}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThere are $6+3+1=10$ subsets.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Consider the subset $\\{A,B\\}$. What letters have been omitted from the subset?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$C,D,E$ have been omitted.",
          "worked": "Removing $A$ and $B$ from $S$ leaves $\\{C,D,E\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Use the definition of ${}^{n}C_r$ to explain why ${}^{5}C_2={}^{5}C_3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Each choice of 2 letters from 5 leaves a unique complementary choice of 3 letters, so ${}^{5}C_2={}^{5}C_3$.",
          "worked": "${}^{5}C_2$ counts the ways to choose 2 letters from 5, and ${}^{5}C_3$ counts the ways to choose 3 letters from 5.\n\nChoosing 2 letters to include is equivalent to choosing 3 letters to exclude. Each 2-letter subset corresponds to exactly one complementary 3-letter subset; for example, $\\{A,B\\}$ corresponds to $\\{C,D,E\\}$.\n\nTherefore, ${}^{5}C_2={}^{5}C_3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Explain why ${}^{n}C_r={}^{n}C_{n-r}$ for any whole numbers $n$ and $r$ with $r\\leq n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Choosing $r$ elements to include uniquely determines the $n-r$ elements to exclude, so ${}^{n}C_r={}^{n}C_{n-r}$.",
          "worked": "From a total of $n$ elements, choosing $r$ items to include is equivalent to choosing $n-r$ items to exclude.\n\nEach $r$-member subset corresponds to exactly one complementary $(n-r)$-member subset, and conversely. The two counts are therefore equal:\n$${}^{n}C_r={}^{n}C_{n-r}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
